Gadgetbridge interoperability references
---------------------------------------
Project: https://codeberg.org/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge
Mirror: https://github.com/Freeyourgadget/Gadgetbridge
Authors: Gadgetbridge contributors, including Jose Rebelo
Upstream license: GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or later

This project reads Gadgetbridge SQLite exports and uses its public Intent API.
Its Xiaomi mappings and Python/JavaScript protocol implementations were informed
by Gadgetbridge's XiaomiHealthService, XiaomiScheduleService, xiaomi.proto,
SleepDetailsParser, DailySummaryParser and database entity definitions.
These are interoperability references; the Gadgetbridge application, source
checkout, generated protocol classes, APKs, icons and artwork are not bundled.

The Python schedule implementation is maintained in
mibandctl/health/schedules.py; upstream references explain protocol values,
while local locking, read-back verification and error handling are implemented
in this repository. This project is independent of Xiaomi and Gadgetbridge.

Runtime dependencies
--------------------
The MCP Python SDK is installed as a dependency from its own distribution:
https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk

The optional Xiaomi Health backend uses Frida. Its runtime installer downloads
a pinned, checksum-verified binary from the official Frida release; the binary
is not included in this repository or its source archive:
https://github.com/frida/frida

Those projects retain their own licenses and copyright notices. See their
respective distributions for the applicable terms.
